06/4499132092","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Restless Legs Syndrome: A Review.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41563785/","source":"JAMA","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Psilocybin in the Treatment of Cocaine Use Disorder: A Randomized Clinical Trial.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42096204/","source":"JAMA network open","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"CAR/CSACI Practice Guidance for Contrast Media Hypersensitivity.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39797723/","source":"Canadian Association of Radiologists journal = Journal l'Association canadienne des radiologistes","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Diphenhydramine, Sodium Bicarbonate, or Combination for Acute Peripheral Vertigo: A Randomized Clinical Trial.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41196596/","source":"JAMA network open","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Standardized Extract of Valeriana officinalis Improves Overall Sleep Quality in Human Subjects with Sleep Complaints: A Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled, Clinical Study.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37899385/","source":"Advances in therapy","year":2024,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"},{"title":"Sedative effects of antihistamines.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2885356/","source":"The Journal of allergy and clinical immunology","year":1987,"cites":null,"kind":"Clinical Trial"},{"title":"Daytime sleepiness and antihistamines.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6146180/","source":"Sleep","year":1984,"cites":null,"kind":"Clinical Trial"},{"title":"One man's poison.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/82859/","source":"Lancet (London, England)","year":1978,"cites":null,"kind":"Clinical Trial"}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"KSman is Here","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/ksman-is-here/186318","site":"T Nation · 999 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Insomnia while on TRT","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/insomnia-while-on-trt/195182","site":"T Nation · 63 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Sleep Deprived? Raise Your Hand","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/sleep-deprived-raise-your-hand/135469","site":"T Nation · 51 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Sleep Remedies on Juice?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/sleep-remedies-on-juice/270664","site":"T Nation · 24 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Drinking on Cycle? Bad Idea?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/drinking-on-cycle-bad-idea/155384","site":"T Nation · 19 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Anything to Track to Help My TRT Doc?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/anything-to-track-to-help-my-trt-doc/177901","site":"T Nation · 16 posts · 2012"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Diphenhydramine - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diphenhydramine"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Sleep & recovery","chain":["Sedating antihistamine","Faster sleep onset","Rested skin and look"],"effect":"indirect","text":"People use these over-the-counter antihistamines to fall asleep faster, with sleep seen as supporting recovery, skin and looks. They are studied for sleep, though the AASM guideline recommends against diphenhydramine for insomnia; appearance effects have not been studied."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Diphenhydramine is a first-generation H1 antihistamine that is a common ingredient in nonprescription sleep aids; the related doxylamine is used similarly [1]. It was discovered in 1943 by George Rieveschl and Fred Huber and was the first FDA-approved prescription antihistamine in the US in 1946 [1].","Guidance on insomnia is cautious: the American Academy of Sleep Medicine recommended against its use in 2017 citing low-quality evidence, and a 2022 network meta-analysis in The Lancet found little evidence to guide its use [1]."],"infobox":[["Drug class","First-generation H1 antihistamine, anticholinergic"],["Routes","Oral"],["Discovered","1943 [1]"],["First approved","1946 (US, prescription) [1]"],["Legal status","OTC in US and Canada, pharmacy medicine in UK [1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Pharmacology","paras":[],"subs":[{"h":"Mechanism of action","paras":["Diphenhydramine acts mainly as an inverse agonist at H1 receptors, and its central effects cause drowsiness. It is also a potent muscarinic antagonist, a sodium channel blocker and a weak serotonin reuptake inhibitor [1]."]}]},{"h":"Adverse effects","paras":["The most common effects are dizziness and sleepiness. Anticholinergic effects include dry mouth, faster heart rate, urinary retention and constipation; higher doses can cause confusion, hallucinations or delirium, and overdose can cause QT prolongation and arrhythmias [1]. Paradoxical excitation occurs, especially in children [1].","Anticholinergic exposure in later life has been linked to cognitive decline and dementia, but a 2019 JAMA Internal Medicine nested case-control study found the strongest associations for other anticholinergic classes and no significantly increased risk for antihistamines [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["Evidence assessments for insomnia are summarised in the 2017 American Academy of Sleep Medicine guideline, which recommended against diphenhydramine, and in a 2022 Lancet network meta-analysis that found little evidence to guide its use [1]. No studies found specifically on appearance outcomes."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Legal status","paras":["Diphenhydramine is over-the-counter in the US and Canada, a pharmacy medicine in the UK, and prescription-only in Sweden; it is unscheduled internationally but prohibited in Zambia [1]."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1943","event":"Discovered at the University of Cincinnati by George Rieveschl and Fred Huber [1]."},{"year":"1946","event":"First FDA-approved prescription antihistamine in the US [1]."},{"year":"2017","event":"AASM guideline recommends against diphenhydramine for insomnia [1]."},{"year":"2019","event":"JAMA Internal Medicine study finds no significant dementia association for antihistamines [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Diphenhydramine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diphenhydramine","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Diphenhydramine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diphenhydramine","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"KSman is Here","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/ksman-is-here/186318","site":"T Nation · 999 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Insomnia while on TRT","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/insomnia-while-on-trt/195182","site":"T Nation · 63 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Sleep Deprived? Raise Your Hand","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/sleep-deprived-raise-your-hand/135469","site":"T Nation · 51 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Sleep Remedies on Juice?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/sleep-remedies-on-juice/270664","site":"T Nation · 24 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Drinking on Cycle? Bad Idea?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/drinking-on-cycle-bad-idea/155384","site":"T Nation · 19 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Anything to Track to Help My TRT Doc?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/anything-to-track-to-help-my-trt-doc/177901","site":"T Nation · 16 posts · 2012"}]}